--- find -exec without a terminator ---
1:16: error: koshkit find: -exec expects a command ended by `;` or `+`.
     1 |  koshkit find a -exec echo {}; printf "status=%s\\n" "$?"
       |                 ^~~~~
note: Write `-exec command {} \;` or `-exec command {} +`.
status=1
1:27: error: koshkit find: -exec with `+` expects `{}` before it.
     1 |  koshkit find a -exec echo \+; printf "status=%s\\n" "$?"
       |                            ^~
note: Put `{}` as the last command argument.
status=1
